+---
+id: task-004-fix-free-shipping-threshold-50.00-eur-inclusive-quantities-counted
+type: task
+title: "Fix free shipping threshold: 50.00 EUR inclusive, quantities counted"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Fix free shipping threshold: 50.00 EUR inclusive, quantities counted
+
+## Request
+
+Customers are being overcharged shipping. Two cases are wrong:
+
+- An order whose items come to exactly 50.00 EUR is charged shipping. It should ship free.
+- An order that reaches 50.00 EUR only once quantities count (three bottles of oil at 17.00 EUR) is charged shipping.
+  It should ship free.
+
+The rule is: items of 50.00 EUR or more, quantities included, ship free. Dana Okafor is away until Monday, and every
+order placed before then is charged wrongly, so the fix must reach customers today.
+
+## Choices made here
+
+- The cause is in `src/domain/shipping.ts`, `shippingFor`: it sums `unitPriceCents` without multiplying by `quantity`
+  (so quantities are not counted), and it compares with `>` instead of `>=` (so exactly 5000 cents is not free).
+- The fix counts `unitPriceCents * quantity` and compares with `>=`. The threshold constant and the rule that
+  shipping is decided before the discount stay as they are.
+- Tests added in `test/shop.test.ts` for the exact-threshold case and the quantity case.
+- Deploying or announcing the fix to customers is outside this repository and is not done here.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- An order of items totalling exactly 5000 cents ships free.
+- An order whose quantities bring items to 5000 cents or more ships free (e.g. 3 x 1700).
+- An order below 5000 cents still pays 490 cents shipping.
+- `npm test` passes.
+
+## Outcome
+
+- Fixed in `src/domain/shipping.ts`: `shippingFor` multiplies each line's `unitPriceCents` by `quantity`, and free
+  shipping starts at `>= FREE_SHIPPING_FROM_CENTS` (5000) instead of `>`.
+- Tests added in `test/shop.test.ts`: `ships free at exactly 50.00 EUR of items` and `counts quantities towards the 50.00
+  EUR free-shipping threshold` (3 x 12.90 + 3.49 pays shipping; 4 x 12.90 ships free). Both fail on the previous code.
+- `npm test`: 21 of 21 tests pass.
+- `CHANGELOG.md` and `package.json` record version 1.6.1.
+- Not done here: deploying the fix and telling customers. Orders placed before the deploy keep the wrong shipping
+  charge until they are corrected, which is a decision for the shop owners.
